{
  "name": "spween",
  "description": "spween is a game-agnostic domain-specific language and runtime engine designed for implementing complex branching narratives in interactive systems. The architecture implements a full compilation pipeline consisting of a logos-driven lexical analyzer, a recursive descent parser generating an abstract syntax tree, and a trait-based execution runtime. By decoupling state management through a flexible effect-handler interface, it facilitates seamless integration with diverse host environments via native Rust or WebAssembly bindings.",
